#packages
```{r}
library(readr)
library(base)
library(here)
library(dplyr)
library(xtable)
library(stargazer)
```

#loading data
```{r}
ches = read.csv(here::here("data", "ches1419.csv"))
ess = read.csv(here::here("data", "ess_cleaned.csv"))
ess$country = NA
ess$country = ess$cntry

#data structure
colnames(ches)
# country, year, party, electionyear, lrgen, galtan, immigrate_policy
table(ches$country)
table(ess$cntry)
```

# dividing dataset
I am subsetting datasets for both ESS and CHES because CHES has two years (2014 and 2019) and it gets complicated if I put them all together.
```{r}
#dataset that will use ches2019
ches_2019 <- ches[ches$year == 2019, ]
ches_2014 <- ches[ches$year == 2014, ]

ess9 = ess[ess$essround %in% 9, ]
ess10 = ess[ess$essround %in% 10, ]
```

#party position coding (based on 2019 CHES)
Let's do step by step. Otherwise, you will burn out. 
1. each country's party list column are coded as numeric.
2. let's change it to party name.
3. let's coalsce those party names into one column party
4. let's match based on party name and country and add party details. 

